---

```
=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: switch_dist_1_1
diagnosis_text:
The fault is a missing OSPF network statement on switch_dist_1_1. The device's FRR
OSPF configuration includes only "network 172.16.0.6/31 area 1", which covers
the transit link to router_core_1 (eth0, 172.16.0.7). The access-side subnet
10.1.1.0/24, hosted on interface br0, is never injected into OSPF and therefore
never advertised to the rest of the topology.

As a result, router_core_1, router_core_2, router_core_3, and switch_dist_2_1
have zero routing knowledge of 10.1.1.0/24. Traffic from host_1_1_1_1 (10.1.1.2)
reaches its gateway switch_dist_1_1 just fine (local L2 hop) and is correctly
forwarded into the core, but return packets destined for 10.1.1.2 arrive at
router_core_1 with no matching FIB entry and are silently dropped. This explains
the exact asymmetry in the ticket: the host can ping its gateway (no routing
needed), switch_dist_1_1 can ping the server farm (its source IP is 172.16.0.7,
which is OSPF-reachable), but host_1_1_1_1 gets no replies to anything beyond
its own /24. Pod 2 is unaffected because switch_dist_2_1 correctly carries both
"network 10.2.1.0/24 area 1" and "network 172.16.0.8/31 area 1".

Root cause: The "network 10.1.1.0/24 area 1" line was never added to
switch_dist_1_1's OSPF stanza.

Corrective fix: On switch_dist_1_1, enter vtysh and add:
  router ospf
    network 10.1.1.0/24 area 1
This will cause switch_dist_1_1 to originate a Type-1 LSA for br0, propagate
10.1.1.0/24 to all OSPF neighbors, and restore full bidirectional reachability
for host_1_1_1_1.
=== END ===
```